List<Integer> nums = Arrays.asList(
        2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19);

List<Integer> result = nums.stream()
        .filter(n -> n < 10)
        .sorted((a, b) -> b - a)
        .limit(4)
        .skip(2)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

out.println(result);

questions.explanation:
Stream operations:  
filter(n -> n < 10) reduces the list to [2, 3, 5, 7]; 
sorted((a,b) -> b-a) reverses to [7, 5, 3, 2];  
limit(4) keeps all 4 elements (no effect); 
skip(2) removes first 2 elements, leaving [3, 2].

